meaning:
Some Rap Songs thematic focus centres on Earl’s relationship with his parents, particularly reconciling with his late father Keorapetse Kgositsile. As Earl navigates through his grief, he is offering a sense of maturity otherwise negated on previous releases, which is exemplified by the importance placed upon family in this line.

Speaking on the closure SRS' release provides, Earl stated;

Talking to him is symbolic and non-symbolic, but it’s literally closure for my childhood. Not getting to have that moment left me to figure out a lot with my damn self.”

Earl draws a paradox of feeling high, or ‘bent', when he’s sober, and sober, or more comfortable with his surroundings, when he’s high. These lines harbour similarities to Earl’s hook on the Frank Ocean assisted cut “Sunday”, released on Doris;

All my dreams got dimmer when I stopped smoking pot
Nightmares got more vivid when I stopped smoking pot"
